# {{AGENT_NAME}} — Slack Triage Agent (operations)

Answers @mentions and DMs grounded in this repository; triages the designated
channels ({{WATCHED_CHANNELS}}); the `:{{TRIGGER_EMOJI}}:` emoji summons it
onto any message. Event-driven — no cron, no servers. Installed by
[ai-automations](https://github.com/makasanaakshay/ai-automation-master);
re-run its installer to update (answers saved in `automation.config.json`).

```
Slack Events API (signed; relay acks <3s, dispatches async)
  → Cloudflare Worker relay            scripts/slack-agent/relay/worker.js
  → repository_dispatch                .github/workflows/slack-agent.yml
  → agent-run.sh                       restore state → resolve thread → playbook → save state
```

| Trigger | Playbook | Output |
|---|---|---|
| @mention anywhere the bot is | `mention` | ONE threaded, grounded answer |
| New message in a watched channel | `triage` | Answer / GitHub issue + link / silence |
| `:{{TRIGGER_EMOJI}}:` reaction on a message | `triage` | Same, explicitly summoned |
| DM to the bot | `dm` | ONE conversational answer |

Enabled handlers: **{{HANDLERS}}**. State lives on the orphan branch
`slack-agent-state` (`state/<channel>-<root_ts>.json`: kind, phase, last_ts,
issue_url). Every run re-fetches the thread and diffs against `last_ts` —
webhook payloads are only doorbells. Loop protection is structural: the bot's
own user id (from `auth.test`) and any `bot_id` messages are never input.

## Operating

- **Re-check a thread:** Actions → *Slack Triage Agent* → *Run workflow* with `item_id` = `<channel>:<root_ts>`; empty re-checks every tracked thread.
- **Transcripts:** every run uploads `.agent-out/` as an artifact.
- **Model:** `AI_MODEL` in `scripts/slack-agent/env.sh` (currently `{{AI_MODEL}}`, brain `{{BRAIN_NAME}}`).
- **Pause:** disable Event Subscriptions in the Slack app config (api.slack.com/apps).
- **Channels/emoji:** `env.sh` **and** the relay's `wrangler.toml` must agree — easiest: re-run the installer, then redeploy the relay.

## Local dry-run (safe — needs SLACK_BOT_TOKEN exported)

```bash
DRY_RUN=1 bash scripts/slack-agent/agent-run.sh                          # tracked threads
DRY_RUN=1 ITEM_ID="C0123:1712345678.000100" bash scripts/slack-agent/agent-run.sh
```

## Guardrails

- Slack writes are **threaded replies only** — never new channel messages, DMs to others, or @channel/@here. GitHub writes are **issues only** — this agent never writes code or opens PRs.
- Channels are conversation: outside watched channels the agent only acts on explicit summons (mention, emoji, DM); chatter gets silence.
- Deliveries are signature-verified (v0 HMAC + timestamp freshness) at the edge; `--dangerously-skip-permissions` only in the disposable CI runner.
